Interpretation:
- We have a new straight route from A to B.
- Existing railway lines are also straight segments, each labeled by company.
- Whenever the new route intersects an existing line, the new route must be:
  - at the same level if the line belongs to Nate's company,
  - at a different level if it belongs to a competitor.
- Along the route, changing between above/underground requires an entrance.
- We want the minimum number of entrances.

